course: dictionary
lesson: 4270
title: Gravy
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Gravy is a noun. It is a hot, brown sauce made from the juices of cooked meat, often thickened with flour. You can use the context around a word to check its meaning. «His grandma dropped her fork, the gravy went everywhere and Ollie lost his pudding.» Gravy that goes everywhere must be runny, so it is a liquid, not a solid food.
explain: The sentence «Grandad and Auntie Jo argue about the government until the gravy goes cold» gives a clue too. Gravy goes cold, so it is served hot, and it is part of a meal with other food. Try the check: swap in the meaning, "until the hot brown sauce goes cold". It still makes sense, so you have found the right meaning.
explain: Look at the joke: «it's not gravy, it's a brown lake.» The brown lake shows that gravy is brown and thin enough to spread out. Gravy is uncountable, so you say some gravy or a jug of gravy, not two gravies.
fact: Gravy is a noun, and it is uncountable: you say some gravy, not two gravies.
fact: Gravy is made from the juices of cooked meat, often thickened with flour.
fact: Gravy is poured over meat, potatoes and other food.
fact: In the southern USA, gravy can also be a white creamy sauce served with biscuits.
fact: «Gravy train» is an informal phrase for an easy way to get money.
exercise: «His grandma dropped her fork, the gravy went everywhere and Ollie lost his pudding.» Which food is gravy? | A sweet cake | *A hot brown sauce | A cold white ice lolly | A crunchy bread roll
exercise: Which sentence uses gravy correctly? | *Please pass the gravy. | Please pass the gravies. | Please pass the gravys. | Please pass three gravy.
exercise: Dad says, «That job is a gravy train.» What does gravy train mean? | *An easy way to get money | A train that carries gravy | A long journey by train | A dinner served on a train
test: In Canada, poutine is chips with cheese curds and what? | ketchup | custard | *gravy | jam
test: Gravy is made from the juices of cooked what? | leaves | paper | sugar | *meat
exam: In which part of the world can gravy be a white creamy sauce served with biscuits? | Antarctica | *Southern USA | Iceland | Central Africa
